# Crockpot API — /recipe-categories
#
# GET is public (no token). POST/PATCH/DELETE are ADMIN-only, gated by
# middleware.RequireRole("ADMIN") — the 401/403 shape of that gate is
# already covered by internal/middleware's own unit tests, so this file
# focuses on the wiring: public read, ADMIN CRUD happy path, and the
# 409/404 translations, run against a live server + real DB.
#
# Unlike /item-categories and /units, there's a single mutable field
# (name) — PATCH always requires it, no partial-update case to exercise.
# The 409 category_in_use delete-guard (recipe_categories_recipes is
# ON DELETE RESTRICT) needs a real recipe row to trigger, which this
# file doesn't create — covered instead by
# internal/repository/recipe_category_test.go's TestDeleteRecipeCategory_InUse.
#
# One-time setup: this repo's dev DB has no ADMIN user yet. Bump the
# same shared test account requests/auth.http / me.http use:
#
#   UPDATE users SET role = 'ADMIN' WHERE email = 'REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL';
#
# Harmless to auth.http / me.http — neither asserts on role. See
# requests/README.md for setup/running instructions.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Login (ADMIN account)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Login, to get a token for the checks below.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL",
  "password": "correcthorsebattery"
}

###

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /recipe-categories (public)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — no token needed, returns the seeded categories ordered by name
GET http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /recipe-categories (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 201 — creates the category this file exercises below
# @name create
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-recipe-category"
}

###

@categoryId = {{create.response.body.id}}

### 🚫 409 name_taken — same name as above
POST http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-recipe-category"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /recipe-categories/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — name is required, no partial-update case for this resource
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "http-test-recipe-category-renamed"
}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — a random id that doesn't exist
PATCH http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "doesn't matter"
}

###


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /recipe-categories/:id (ADMIN)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 204 — deletes the category created above (also this file's cleanup)
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### 🚫 404 not_found — already deleted by the request above
DELETE http://localhost:{{$dotenv PORT}}/recipe-categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  Cleanup
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### Nothing dangling: the ✅ 204 delete above already removes the one
### category this file creates, so a re-run from a clean server behaves
### the same way twice.
###
### Optional — revert the one-time ADMIN bump if you don't want the
### shared test account staying ADMIN:
#
#   UPDATE users SET role = 'FREE' WHERE email = 'REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_EMAIL';
#
